3. **Its tests** — create `.github/scripts/test_skia_archive.py`, stdlib `unittest`, one `TestCase` per function
   (architecture S1). It drives the script's functions with a temporary record and `file://` source URLs (urllib reads
   them), never the network. Cases:
   - a matching local copy is reused, with no fetch;
   - a fetched archive whose sum matches is renamed into place and its URL printed;
   - a mismatched archive is refused with exit 1, and no file is left at the archive's path;
   - a source failing twice then succeeding is fetched on attempt 3;
   - a source failing three times exits 1 after three attempts, with three attempt lines;
   - an unrecorded target exits 2 before any fetch;
   - success prints exactly one line and nothing on stderr;
   - the committed record holds the five targets of step 1, its row count asserted (tests S5);
   - every `sha256` is 64 hex digits;
   - the record's `tag` equals `Cargo.lock`'s `skia-bindings` version, read through `test_cargo_lock.py`'s
     `parse_lock`, so a skia move reddens until the sums move by hand (inputs#I2 §1a).

   Each case is controlled red-before-green (tests S5).

- (security) The eleven advisory IDs are enumerated once each in `evidence/advisory-standing.md` (gate 7, last line
  11):
  - zip ×4 closed;
  - sqlite, paste, zbus ×3, ttf-parser and memmap2 each a wait on a named release (F1 A, F3 A: inputs#I4);
  - none left without an outcome.
  This is `matrix#v040-07`'s advisory half.

- (security / CI) The verified archive (inputs#I2 §1a):
  - `python3 .github/scripts/test_skia_archive.py` reads OK, a mismatched archive refused and no file left;
  - the record's tag is held to the lock's `skia-bindings`;
  - `python3 .github/scripts/test_ci_workflows.py` reads OK, every `SKIA_LEGS` leg running cargo under
    `FORCE_SKIA_BINARIES_DOWNLOAD=1` and the matrix step pinned on every row;
  - after `bash .github/scripts/ci-leg.sh fast`, the dev host's skia-bindings build output names a `FROM: file://`
    URL (gate 5) `(security-plan · dependency-security/skia-default-build-fetch)`.

- (codebase) gated: `matrix#v040-08`. The Epoch 2 boundary audit, recorded as its metric row (the gated entry), reads:
  - the stand tests' duplication back under its earlier reading;
  - each oversize file and over-ceiling function under its bar or kept by the founder's word (inputs#I2 §4–7);
  - the browser's four mutants caught or kept;
  - every check green.

  `gated: the Epoch 2 boundary audit of escher-0.4.0 recorded, its reading cleared by the operator word (CARRY
  cry-hpakkesz; inputs#I3)`.

- Spec anchors:
  - `(security-plan · dependency-security/advisory-ignores-by-id)`, `(security-plan · dependency-security/audit-ignores-per-id-with-reason)`,
    `(security-plan · dependency-security/skia-default-build-fetch)`, `(security-plan · dependency-security/dependency-audit-cargo-deny)`,
    `(security-plan · dependency-security/locked-builds)`, `(security-plan · authentication-authorization/ci-token-read-only)`,
    `(security-plan · dependency-security/ci-actions-pinned-to-sha)`, `(security-plan · secret-management/environment-variables/ci)`;
  - `(architecture · standard-contracts/one-ci-leg-runner)`, `(architecture · stack-and-technologies/local-pre-push-gate)`,
    `(architecture · standard-contracts/ci-contract-pinned)`, `(architecture · infrastructure-patterns/ci-read-only-permissions)`;
  - `(test-plan · ci-integration/package-installs-bounded-and-retried)`, `(test-plan · ci-integration/build-directory-held-by-sweep)`,
    `(test-plan · 1-test-scope-summary/native-platform-ci-matrix)`;
  - `(obs-plan · 9-ci-integration/fork-ci-two-artifacts)` — the archive is uploaded by no job;
  - `(a11y-plan · a11y-scope-summary/stand-builds-no-platform-adapter)`;
  - `(design-system · surface/mobile-targets-built-not-tested)` — the matrix keeps building ios and android.

- Words:
  - the founder's ruling (verified archive), «Проверенный архив (Recommended)», inputs#I2 §1a;
  - the operator's directive, inputs#I1;
  - the operator's technical answers, inputs#I3 (the operator, 2026-11-21);
  - F1 A · F2 A · F3 A, inputs#I4 — delegate the operator, 2026-11-21, PROVISIONAL, standing for the founder's own
    word, which supersedes it by rule.

- Beyond the plan, rows for the P5 card:
  - a cross-version residual row owning the RUSTSEC-2026-0192 ignore (a wait on the winit 0.31 beta chain), minted at
    the wrap, with its id re-pointed into `deny.toml`'s reason by a CARRY on «Upstream sync ahead of the canvas»;
  - the residual dispositions of this cap's six rows at the wrap:
    - `res-h7acz56c` closed, fixed;
    - `res-q2tllspz` retired by its rule;
    - `res-j4x7iiqc`, `res-kdhnfj5p`, `res-p73cueyv` and `res-uqt2yd2y` re-carried as stated waits.

- (security / CI) The verified archive (inputs#I2 §1a):
  - `python3 .github/scripts/test_skia_archive.py` reads OK, a mismatched archive refused and no file left;
  - the record's tag is held to the lock's `skia-bindings`;
  - `python3 .github/scripts/test_ci_workflows.py` reads OK, every `SKIA_LEGS` leg running cargo under
    `FORCE_SKIA_BINARIES_DOWNLOAD=1` and the matrix step pinned on every row;
  - after `bash .github/scripts/ci-leg.sh fast`, the dev host's skia-bindings build output names a `FROM: file://`
    URL (gate 5) `(security-plan · dependency-security/skia-default-build-fetch)`;
  - before any CI run, all five recorded archives are fetched from their release URLs on this host by the script
    itself and verified against the record (gate 8, last line 5). `evidence/skia-archives-measured.md` holds five
    lines, each the sha256 the script computed beside the published digest, `equal` (gate 9, last line 5).

- **Symbols / APIs:**
  - `skia_archive.py` (new, stdlib Python ≥ 3.11 `tomllib`, reads no environment variable):
    - functions `load_record`, `sha256_of`, `archive_path`, `url_template`, `fetch_to`, `verified_archive`, `main`
      (`skia_archive.py:31-101`, new-text listing);
    - CLI `skia_archive.py TARGET DIR`: exit 0 and one stdout line, the `SKIA_BINARIES_URL` template
      `file://{DIR resolved, POSIX form}/skia-binaries-{key}.tar.gz` with `{key}` literal for skia-bindings to fill;
    - exit 1 with fixed stderr lines `skia-archive: attempt {n} of 3 failed in {fetch|verify}` then
      `skia-archive: no verified archive`;
    - exit 2 with `skia-archive: usage` or `skia-archive: no recorded archive for this target`, nothing fetched;
    - fetch: `urllib.request` with a 120 s timeout, 3 attempts 10 s apart, into a `.skia-archive-*.part` temporary
      file in DIR, renamed into place only when its sha256 equals the record; a matching local copy is reused with
      no fetch.
  - `ci-leg.sh`:
    - `SKIA_LEGS=(clippy test build msrv doc coverage a11y)`;
    - `in_list` (`ci-leg.sh:20-27`);
    - `use_verified_skia` (`ci-leg.sh:29-36`), which runs the script for `rustc -vV`'s host into
      `target/skia-archives` and exports `SKIA_BINARIES_URL`;
    - `run_leg` calls it first for a leg in `SKIA_LEGS` (`ci-leg.sh:39-41`), and a non-zero exit ends the leg before
      any cargo runs;
    - the fast arm's sweep call runs as `{ use_verified_skia && python3 …/target-sweep.py run; } || true`
      (`ci-leg.sh:112-115`).
    `FORCE_SKIA_BINARIES_DOWNLOAD` is set nowhere.
  - Env vars: `SKIA_BINARIES_URL` is set by the leg runner and by the matrix step, read by skia-bindings' build
    script. It holds no secret, a local `file://` path template.

- **Counts / qualifiers moved:**
  - the leg runner's skia-building legs: 7 legs, `SKIA_LEGS` (new);
  - the `ci-scripts` leg gains `test_skia_archive.py` (unittest discovery);
  - the matrix job's steps gain two: `Verified skia archive` and `Skia built from the verified archive`.

- **Harness / gate surface:**
  - `ci-leg.sh`'s skia arm and the sweep under the verified URL;
  - `ci.yml` `matrix_test`, after `Setup`: `Verified skia archive` (`shell: bash`; `python` on windows-latest,
    `python3` elsewhere; appends `SKIA_BINARIES_URL={line}` to `$GITHUB_ENV`);
  - after `test`: `Skia built from the verified archive` (`shell: bash`), which exits 1 unless one
    `target/{target}/debug/build/skia-bindings-*/output` holds both `FROM: file://` and
    `DOWNLOAD AND INSTALL SUCCEEDED`, printing `skia-archive: no skia-bindings build read the verified archive`;
  - no action, permission or `secrets.` added.

- (security / CI) the verified archive:
  - unit tests OK, a mismatched archive refused with no file left — **met** (gate 1; control `sum-unchecked` holds);
  - the tag held to the lock — **met**;
  - `test_ci_workflows.py` OK, every `SKIA_LEGS` leg running cargo under the verified URL, the matrix step pinned on
    every row — **met**, re-worded: under `SKIA_BINARIES_URL` and NOT `FORCE_SKIA_BINARIES_DOWNLOAD` (inputs#I7;
    gate 2; control `url-unexported` holds);
  - the dev host's skia-bindings output names `FROM: file://` — **met** (gate 5, firing 4);
  - all five archives fetched and verified before any CI run — **met** (gate 8 last line 5, gate 9 last line 5).
